{
  "assessment": "The change introduces safeGet but leaves a critical traversal bug: accessing properties on null or undefined intermediate values still throws a TypeError during iteration, despite correctly preserving terminal falsy values like 0 and false. The fix only guards the final return statement rather than validating each step of the path, meaning it fails the core requirement to handle missing paths gracefully.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "actual": "Throws TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'b')",
      "at": "solution.mjs:5 (current = current[part] inside loop)",
      "call": "node --input-type=module -e \"import {safeGet} from './solution.mjs'; safeGet({a: null}, 'a.b', 'default')\"",
      "defect": "Intermediate traversal lacks null/undefined safety check",
      "expected": "Logs 'default' without error"
    }
  ]
}
